<!-- [v7.0 EN Sync] -->
<div class="lf-trap-card" data-trap="T4" data-hq-id="LF-T4-P5-1206">
            <div class="lf-trap-header">
                <span class="lf-trap-badge">T4</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-diff">⭐⭐⭐ 🔴</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-id">LF-T4-P5-1206</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Find the area of a square inscribed in a circle using the radius of the circle. (radius = r)</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> r²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> The diagonal of the square = 2r, side length = 2r/√2, area = 2r²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T4+T5 The side length of an inscribed square ≠ the radius
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Inside a circle there is a regular hexagon. Each side of the hexagon has length = the radius r of the circle. Find the perimeter of the hexagon.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 2πr
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 6r (perimeter of the hexagon, not the circle)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T4 Read carefully which shape the question is asking about! Do not apply the circle formula to a polygon.
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">In the formula for the area of a circle, the radius is 5 cm. Find the area. (π=3.14)</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 2×3.14×5=31.4
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 3.14×5²=78.5 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T4+T5 πr² vs 2πr (area vs circumference)
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A semicircle (with the diameter as the base) has a diameter of 10cm. Find the perimeter. (π=3.14)</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span>π×10÷2=15.7cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span>π×10÷2+10=15.7+10=25.7cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span>T4+T5 Perimeter of a semicircle = semicircular arc + diameter
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">The radius of a circle is 7cm. Find the circumference. (π=22/7)</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span>π×7=22cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span>2×π×7=44cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span>T4 Circumference = 2πr, not πr (that is for a semicircle)
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A circular garden has a diameter of 14m. There is a 1m wide path around the garden. Find the circumference of the path. (π=22/7)</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span>π×14=44m
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span>π×(14+2)=π×16=352/7≈50.29m
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span>T4 The question asks for the circumference of the path (not the garden) → must add the path width
                </div>

                <div class="trap-mantra">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Mnemonic:</span>"When there are several numbers in the question, first check clearly which one is being asked"
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Cut a right-angled triangle (with legs equal to the width and part of the length) from a rectangle. Find the remaining area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake:</span> Forgetting to divide the triangle area by 2.
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Answer:</span> Rectangle area minus triangle area.
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap Analysis:</span> T4+T5 Dividing the triangle area by 2 is an eternal trap.
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A small triangle is cut out from a large triangle (the two triangles are similar but do not overlap). Find the remaining area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake:</span> Large area minus small area, but the small area is calculated incorrectly.
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Answer:</span> Calculate each area separately, then subtract.
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap Analysis:</span> T4 The base and height of the two triangles must be confirmed separately.
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Given an irregular pentagon (all side lengths are marked), find the area using the partition method.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake:</span> After partitioning, the height of one part is matched to the wrong base.
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Answer:</span> Partition correctly → find the area of each part separately → add them together.
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap Analysis:</span> T4+T5 Matching the base and height after partitioning.
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A rectangle is 12 cm long and 8 cm wide. A square with side length 4 cm is cut out from the middle. Find the remaining area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 12 × 8 = 96, then subtract 4 = 92
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 96 − 16 = 80 cm² (subtract the square's area 4 × 4 = 16, not 4)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T4 Subtraction method: what is subtracted is the area, not the side length
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">An L-shaped composite figure (side lengths given). Find the area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> Adding all side lengths directly
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> Divide it into two rectangles, find each area, then add them together
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T4+T5 Matching side lengths in the division method
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">The two adjacent sides of a parallelogram are 10 cm and 6 cm. The height corresponding to the 10 cm base is 4.8 cm. What is the height corresponding to the 6 cm base?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> Also 4.8 cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> Area = 10 × 4.8 = 48 cm², 48 ÷ 6 = 8 cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 Area conservation: different bases correspond to different heights
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A right-angled trapezoid has an upper base of 5 cm, a lower base of 9 cm, and a right-angled side (the height) of 6 cm. What is the height on the slanted side?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 6 cm (directly using the right-angled side)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> Area = (5+9)×6÷2 = 42 cm², height on slanted side = 42×2 ÷ length of slanted side
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 The height on the slanted side ≠ the right-angled side. Area is constant → different bases correspond to different heights
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">The area of a parallelogram is 48 cm² and its height is 6 cm. How long is the base?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 48×6=288cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 48÷6=8 cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 Area ÷ height = base (reverse use of the formula)
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">An isosceles right triangle has two equal sides each 8 cm long. Find the area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 8×8=64 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 8×8÷2 = 32 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 The two legs of a right triangle are the base and height, but we still need to ÷2
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">The area of a trapezoid is 72 cm², and the sum of the top base and bottom base is 18 cm. Find the height.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 72÷18=4cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 72×2÷18 = 8 cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5+T3 Reverse finding height: height = area × 2 ÷ (top base + bottom base)
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A parallelogram has base 8m and height 5m. If the base stays the same and the height becomes 2 times the original, what is the new area?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> Original area × 2 then × 2 again
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 8×(5×2)=80m² (2 times the original area of 40m²)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 Base unchanged, only height changes → Area is proportional to height
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">The area of a triangle is 36 cm², and the base is 9 cm. What is the height?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 36÷9=4cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 36×2÷9 = 8 cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5+T3 Finding height from area → Reverse: height = area × 2 ÷ base
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A trapezoid has a top base of 4cm, a bottom base of 6cm, and a height of 5cm. Find its area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 4×6×5÷3 (randomly applying formula)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> (4+6)×5÷2 = 25 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 Formula confusion: Trapezoid = (top base + bottom base) × height ÷ 2
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A triangle has a base of 10cm and a height of 6cm. Find its area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 60 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 10×6÷2 = 30 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 Forgot to ÷2
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A parallelogram has a base of 12cm and a height of 8cm. A triangle has the same base and height. How many times the area of the triangle is the area of the parallelogram?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common mistake:</span> 1 time (thinking same base and height means same area)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct answer:</span> 2 times
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap analysis:</span> T5 Triangle needs ÷2, parallelogram does not
                </div>

                <div class="trap-mantra">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Mnemonic:</span> "Triangle must divide by 2, parallelogram doesn't need to, same base and height gives double"
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
</body>
</html>